{"type":"message","id":"f28f6df7","parentId":"2db0765c","timestamp":"2026-05-19T08:51:27.386Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both /message and /api/send returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" but not a proper send confirmation. That's odd - they accepted the request but may not have actually sent the message. The history endpoint was a GET, not POST.\n\nLet me try a different approach. Maybe the POST body needs to be in a different format. Let me try with form data.\n\nActually, the fact that it returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" for a POST suggests it might just be responding with a simple text greeting for any POST request. Let me try with a GET to the send endpoint to see if there's a different way.\n\nWait, actually it could be that the platform uses a GET-based send mechanism. \n\nLet me check the docs to understand how this is supposed to work.\n\nActually, I'm wondering if the `/send` endpoint just isn't functional or if there's a different way to invoke it. Let me see if the history endpoint reveals anything about the expected API structure.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-fb132ffc-cef4-43b0-8b40-b827fa9329c2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 08:45 UTC] Test message.\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2bd32ebd-9515-490d-a4ee-5c6006f1f9f3","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":19649,"output":356,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20117,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"ca